# Style, Errors, and Logging

## Code style
- Prefer small methods with clear names.
- Avoid side effects in mapping / conversion code.
- Prefer constructor injection.

## Exceptions and error handling
- Use existing domain exceptions / error model in the repo.
- Do not throw generic RuntimeException unless the repo standard does.
- Keep error messages actionable (what failed, why, what input caused it).

## Logging
- Use the repository’s logging style and levels.
- Never log secrets or personal data.
- Log at boundaries (infrastructure/adapters), not deep in domain logic.
